decoded text, default (unicode_strings, from use v5.36):
                                         \w    \d    \s
U+0041 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER A            yes   no    no
U+00E9 LATIN SMALL LETTER E WITH ACUTE   yes   no    no
U+0301 COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT            yes   no    no
U+0660 ARABIC-INDIC DIGIT ZERO           yes   yes   no
U+FF11 FULLWIDTH DIGIT ONE               yes   yes   no
U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE                    no    no    yes
U+3000 IDEOGRAPHIC SPACE                 no    no    yes

the /a flag restricts the same pattern to ASCII:
  U+0041 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER A            \w yes  \d no
  U+00E9 LATIN SMALL LETTER E WITH ACUTE   \w no   \d no
  U+0301 COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT            \w no   \d no
  U+0660 ARABIC-INDIC DIGIT ZERO           \w no   \d no
  U+FF11 FULLWIDTH DIGIT ONE               \w no   \d no
  U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE                    \w no   \d no
  U+3000 IDEOGRAPHIC SPACE                 \w no   \d no

characters up to U+00FF without the unicode_strings feature (pre-5.12):
  U+0041 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER A            \w yes  \s no
  U+00E9 LATIN SMALL LETTER E WITH ACUTE   \w no   \s no
  U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE                    \w no   \s no

the same twelve characters of text, decoded and not decoded:
  decoded text  length 12   \b\w+\b -> 2   na\u00EFve reader
  raw UTF-8     length 13   \b\w+\b -> 3   na\xC3 ve reader

a number that \d accepts and arithmetic does not (U+0660 U+0661 U+0662):
  =~ /^\d+$/   -> yes
  =~ /^\d+$/a  -> no
  0 + $n       -> 0
  sprintf %d   -> 0
